XIDENTIFYING AMULETS:
X
XIdentifying amulets is a process of elimination, starting with determining
Xwhether or not the amulet is cursed.  Determining whether it's cursed is easy
Xenough if you're a priest or have a pet on hand.  If the amulet is cursed,
Xdon't wear it - there are too many nasty things cursed amulets can do.  If the
Xamulet isn't cursed, it's probably either an amulet of esp, life saving,
Xreflection, or versus poison.  However, watch out - amulets of change often
Xaren't cursed.  So, if you don't mind risking the possibility of changing
Xsexes (and character name), try it on and see what it does.  To see if it's an
Xamulet of esp, get blinded (put on a blindfold, quaff a potion of blindness,
Xetc.).  If you can suddenly see all the monsters on the level, that's what it
Xis.  Next, find a room away from all the monsters, and zap a wand at the wall
Xso that it bounces at you (do this with a wand that you're immune to, or
Xsomething non-harmful like a sleep ray).  If your medallion reflects the ray,
Xit's an amulet of reflection.  Finally, try eating something poisonous.  If it
Xdoesn't do you any harm, it's vs. poison.  If none of these are the case, you
Xknow it's an amulet of life saving - one of the most valuable items in the
Xgame.
