X* Determining your chances for successfully enchanting armor is fairly simple.
XYour chance for succeeding (and not causing the item to disintegrate due to
Xover enchantment) is totally dependent upon the current bonus of the item.  If
Xthe current bonus is three or less (five or less for elven mithril coats), you
Xwill always succeed.  Otherwise, you have one chance out of whatever the
Xcurrent bonus of the item is.  In other words, if the bonus is +4, you have a
X1/4 or 25% chance of being successful.  If the bonus is +8, you have a 1/8 or
X12.5% chance of being successful.  Thus, it is theoretically possible to
Xenchant armor up to +maxint, but the laws of probability would not favor it!
X
X** Chances for successfully enchanting weapons are far easier.  Basically, you
Xwill always succeed if the weapon is at +5 or less.  Once you're over that,
Xyou have a 2/3 chance of being successful each time, regardless of the bonus.
